 First, notice $x^{2n} + 1 + (x+1)^{2n}$ is divisible by $x^2 + x + 1$.  The roots of $x^2 + x + 1 = 0$ are $w, w^2$.  Thus, evaluating the above expression at $w, w^2$, we obtain
\begin{align*}
(-1)^n + 1 + 0 &= 0 \\
(-1)^n + 1 + (-1)^{2n} &= 0
\end{align*}
which gives $n \equiv 1 \pmod{2}$ hence $n = 1, 3, 5, \cdots, 99$.  A typo is easily corrected if $x^2 + x + 1$ gets flipped.  Continue to think to answer. </think>   حياOUS <answer> 50  </answer>

